      "raw": "<p>I&#39;ll throw up what I&#39;ve got right now.&nbsp; Inevitible caveat: I have no idea what I&#39;m doing.&nbsp; I did a little photo editing years ago, but it was nothing fancy, and I downloaded GIMP literally yesterday to take a crack at this.&nbsp; So, advice is very welcome, but don&#39;t mistake me for anything that I&#39;m not.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I&#39;ve uploaded my changes to Beacon&#39;s &quot;portrait&quot;.&nbsp; As I mentioned, that orange and yellow next to each other like that really othered me, so I swapped in Legacy blue.&nbsp; Things I intend to do:</p><ul><li>Restore the orange so people can give Pauline pants without any other changes.</li><li>Swap the placement of the blue and the yellow (except for the sash) - it goes against my instincts to move the bright color adjacent to the white, but I like how her emblem has rays of light emmenating from the &quot;B&quot; (evoking the Legacy lamp), and rays of blue lose that a bit.</li><li>Try the above, only having orange radiating from the B, with blue replacing yellow.&nbsp; Sadly, that means I&#39;ll have to change the color of the sash one way or the other, which suuuuuucks.</li><li>Once I do all of those, if there&#39;s one of the latter two I like more than this version, weep bitter tears and change the other two images to match.&nbsp; Tears grow especially bitter for the one I am half-way through tweaking more extensively.</li></ul>",
